<p class="pnote">Every 3-bit word is a corner of a cube; an edge is one bit-flip. Our code uses just two valid words — <code>000</code> and <code>111</code>, the far corners (teal). Click any corner to "receive" it through a noisy channel: the decoder snaps it to the nearest valid word by majority vote. One error is always corrected; the cube shows you why.</p>

